# waysconf.szymonpaluch.com — one address for the whole session.
#
# The deck and the finished festival site are separate Netlify deploys, so these are
# redirects rather than proxies: both are single-page apps built for the root of their own
# host, and proxying them under a subpath would break every asset URL they emit.
#
# 302 rather than 301 on purpose. A permanent redirect is cached by browsers for a long
# time, and these targets will move again after the conference.

/deck      https://turbine-deck.netlify.app/       302
/deck/*    https://turbine-deck.netlify.app/:splat 302
/site      https://turbine-festival.netlify.app/   302
/site/*    https://turbine-festival.netlify.app/:splat 302

# The prompts page moved when the site was split into two tabs. Anyone holding the old
# link — it was in an early draft of the organiser email — lands in the right place.
/prompts   /workshop/                              301
/prompts/* /workshop/                              301
